;; Problem statements, one per stage of the run, written before the stage is built (docs/RICH-HICKEY.md,
;; "And the hammock."): the problem, the information it needs that the bot does not yet gather, what
;; can go wrong, what done means in world terms, and what the last recorded failure showed. Hand-written
;; data next to goals.edn; problems_test requires a statement for every target goal and checks every
;; source exists. Stages already built cite our own recorded failures; stages ahead cite the siblings
;; (steve, ruststeve), whose notes in brain/siblings are research drafts until re-verified.
;; Update a row when a run of that stage fails in a new way: the failure is the most valuable line here.
[{:problem/stage :wood
  :problem/goals [:wood]
  :problem/statement
  "Hold one log from a natural tree, starting wherever the bot lands, with only what the server has sent it."
  :problem/needs
  ["Which loaded blocks are logs, and which log of a trunk is at feet height."
   "Where its own drop is, and whether a leaf covers it."
   "Whether the landing itself is usable: not water, not inside a canopy, not buried."]
  :problem/risks
  ["A drop lands under the trunk, out of a 1.8-tall player's reach."
   "A branch passes for a trunk bottom, or the trunk stands on a bank above the bot: the drop rests out of the pickup box."
   "A leaf at head height hides the drop and walking cannot pass it."
   "The fixture lands the bot on a pond, in a canopy or in stone."
   "An early FINISH aborts the break."]
  :problem/done "The server's inventory read for the bot shows any *_log."
  :problem/last-failure
  "Recorded in CI and replayed: collect failed :not-picked-up when the bot dug the base log from two blocks above (fixed by trunk-target), and again when a low oak leaf covered the drop (fixed by digging the blocker). Recorded live 2026-10-10 on a pickaxe run and diagnosed by folding the recording: three collects in a row failed :not-picked-up because the drop lay one block up a ledge with leaves one above head height over the ledge and over the bot, so no jump rose a full block (fixed: over a one-block step, the blocker also looks one above the head, in both columns). Recorded by the gym (batch wood-a2 run 5) and again by a plan (smoke2 run 5), landing 21280,18720, and diagnosed by folding the recording: the bot took a branch log (air under it) for a trunk bottom and its drop came to rest on the trunk below; then, standing in a pit, it dug the real base on a bank four blocks above its feet and that drop rested above its pickup box; each failed walk blacklisted one log, not the tree, so it kept choosing the same trunk until the plan failed :stuck. Fixed: a trunk bottom stands on ground (or over its own dug base), a log walk arrives only with the drop's resting height within pickup reach of the feet, and a failed log intent blacklists its whole trunk (sim scenarios a-drop-out-of-reach-is-never-dug-for and a-trunk-on-a-bank-is-taken-from-the-bank). The forest property now generates branches and banks 1-2 high; a tree on a 2-high bank holds its drop beyond a pickup from the ground, and the bot gives it up (:no-log when it is the only tree). Open: cut a step into a bank to stand level with its trunk. The walk now follows a planned route (issue #4): a pond or a two-block ledge between the bot and the trunk, which ended :stuck and blacklisted the trunk, is routed around or climbed by its step (sim scenario a-log-across-a-cliff-and-a-pond-is-reached-by-a-route). Race 38477665442 (issue #38, 39 bots, and the sim race in the same worlds): every bot landed on snowy ground never moved, twelve walks failing :no-path in a second, because one layer of snow lay on every block round it and a route took that layer for an awkward shape, so neither the feet cell nor any beside it could be stood on and every plan was :none from nowhere. Fixed: one layer of snow has no collision shape in the game and the physics passes through it, so a route does too (path/one-layer-snow; path-test a-snowfield-is-crossed-through-its-one-layer-snow). Race 38477665442 (2026-10-13, issue #57, 20 real runs): bots Clj_r14 and Clj_r20 and their runners' twins landed on a lake's shore with every remembered trunk across the water; each walk at one failed :no-path, and once every trunk in reach was given up the gather waited :no-log until the plan failed, the forest beyond the hill never loaded. Under the open sky with no route to any trunk the gather now hunts toward the nearest log, as a water hunt goes out, forty blocks at a time (wood/hunt). Race 38665691517 (issue #57): landings with no standing trunk in reach waited :no-log at the landing round after round, routes out on three bearings; the wood hunt now sets out with no log known (wood/hunt). Race 38680745815 runner 5 (issue #57, 2026-10-15): with 25 bots and two servers to a runner the loop got 9 ticks in 21 s and the wait's wall clock failed the plan :no-log while the water trap's 20 ticks and the hunt's next routable hop were still owed theirs — the wait now fails in planner ticks (plan/wait-ticks) — and once a hop had left the landing, every bearing back toward the then-remembered trunks was refused as nearer the landing; a hunt that knows its trees may walk them (scoop/hunt-targets homeward?)."
  :problem/sources
  ["brain/bot/gotchas/drop-under-the-trunk.md" "brain/bot/gotchas/leaf-canopy-over-the-drop.md"
   "brain/bot/tooling/harness-landing.md" "brain/bot/gotchas/early-finish-aborts.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :kit
  :problem/issue 2
  :problem/goals [:kit]
  :problem/statement
  "Turn logs into a crafting table and four sticks through the 2x2 grid, believing only what the server says the window holds."
  :problem/needs
  ["The recipes, as data from the server jar."
   "Window 0 as the server sees it: grid, cursor and state id, separate from the inventory."
   "Which stack each ingredient comes from, chosen before the first click."]
  :problem/risks ["Leftover planks in the grid craft a button or pressure plate."
                  "A no-op click gets no answer and the craft stalls."
                  "The cursor model and the server's record of it disagree."
                  "A lost or lagged click leaves the grid dirty."]
  :problem/done
  "The server's inventory read shows a crafting_table and four sticks; the grid and cursor are empty."
  :problem/last-failure
  "Verified live on 26.1.2: after the put-back click the bot still believed a stack was on the cursor, clicked an empty slot to drop it, got no answer and failed :stale-window (fixed by dropping the cursor on every click, as the 775 server does). Sim race 38515210080 (issue #104, 19 runs, world R2/45) and race 38515209959 (4 real bots, the table in hand and the last intent its craft): the first log came down into a crevice of the forest floor two deep under its own canopy, and the sticks sent the bot for a second with the trunk two blocks off; a level step ran along the crevice's floor and the leaves over it are not cover, so stairs/out? said out, the one notch up ended under the leaves, no route reached a trunk or a hunt's ground, and it waited :no-log. The same false out as #102's quarry, fixed with it (stairs/pit-rim); plan-test a-crevice-under-the-canopy-is-climbed-out-of holds the crevice, and the snapshots of R2/45 under test/issues/104 the check. Played on (PR #114's issue check) R2-45-2 and R2-45-3 still failed: one stair up put the bot in a notch one deep under the leaves, every column round it had a cell to stand in a block up, so stairs/pit-rim took the notch for open ground, the climb ended and the wait began again. A step up needs the jump's headroom (stairs/step-rises): with leaves two over the feet no column a block up counts as stepped into, and the notch is still a pit."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/01-crafting-as-data.md"
