 {:problem/stage :nether-and-fortress
  :problem/issue 11
  :problem/goals [:fortress]
  :problem/statement
  "The world value is overworld-only, so after a portal the bot cannot tell which dimension it is in, decodes Nether chunks with the wrong height, and has no safe way to reach a fortress across the lava sea."
  :problem/needs
  ["The dimension from login and respawn (sent as a registry index, 3 = the_nether)"
   "Per-dimension chunk height: Nether is min-y 0, 16 sections; overworld -64, 24 sections"
   "Sightings keyed by dimension, watching nether_bricks, spawner, portal, obsidian and lava"
   "Real chunk data after arrival before any step runs, not a timer"
   "Lava next to each tunnel step and missing floors ahead"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["Chunks stay a snapshot of the dimension the bot is in, emptied on a change, as the server streams them again; memory keeps every dimension, each fact saying which"
   "A column's height is the sections the server sent (16 or 24), looked up in dimensions.edn: the reader thread decodes without knowing the dimension"
   "The dimension is the respawn's and login's name (:player/dimension, from #8), not the registry id, which only dimensions.edn's row order explains"
   "No lava capping: a cell behind a wall cannot be capped before the wall is dug, so a tunnel step never opens a cell beside lava and tries another step instead"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Stale overworld columns answer Nether lookups (a brick reported exactly 64 blocks off)"
   "Parsing a Nether chunk as 24 sections runs off the buffer"
   "Overworld goals (mine iron) run in the Nether"
   "Falling into the lava sea on an open approach to the fortress"
   "Fortress brick picked below the lava sea surface"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON confirms the bot is in minecraft:the_nether with nether_bricks under its feet or within 6 blocks, RESULT :ok true, and zero deaths counted."
  :problem/last-failure
  "clojurecraft has never attempted this. ruststeve: after entering the Nether its overworld columns answered Nether lookups (fortress brick reported 64 blocks too low) and the parser panicked on the shorter Nether chunk; finding the fortress was solved, but reaching it alive was not, with 9+ falls into the lava sea at one spot."
  :problem/sources ["docs/issues/09-nether-and-fortress.md" "brain/bot/plan/roadmap-issues.md"
                    "brain/siblings/sib-dimension-change.md"]}
